--- A handle — a mailer, a socket, a stream, a connection, a response — is
--- one kind to the language (spec, Type System: Handles): shown as its
--- word, moved not copied, held by a name and read again, equal to no
--- other. (Each had been a type of its own in the compiler, with a list
--- of the kinds at every rule; docs/extending-crow.md, section 8.)
use web.mail

m = smtp['smtp.example.com', 587, 'ops@example.com', 'secret']
log[type[m]]
log[str[m]]
log[m]
kept = m
log[type[kept]]
mailers = push[[], m]
log[len[mailers]]
